---
description: How to change this repository without disturbing unrelated work
alwaysApply: true
---

# Change discipline

- Read the relevant implementation before editing it.
- Report the files that will change, and keep the edit scoped to the request.
- Do not reformat unrelated sections or files.
- Do not delete existing content or assets without explicit authorization.
- Preserve user-authored uncommitted changes.
- Verify existing behavior after a change.
- Explain any new dependency, configuration file, or architectural decision.

# Legacy code

- New and modified code must meet the project standards.
- Fix a directly adjacent violation only when that fix is safe and necessary.
- Do not rewrite unrelated legacy code to satisfy a new linter.
- Use a targeted lint override only when it is justified, and record the reason in `LEGACY.md`.
- Do not disable an important rule globally to hide existing problems.
- Do not create a formatting-only diff across the repository.
